  ],
  "kind": "extracted",
  "note": "legacy pre-flattening items: composite key (item_id << 16) | damage. Exactly ONE row per item id, named with the era's own registry key and damage 0. minecraft-data carries a 'variations' list per item; it is deliberately NOT expanded into per-damage identifiers, because those identifiers do not exist on these servers. This builder used to emit them as '<name>_<damage>' (dye_5, coal_1, fish_2, flower_pot_9, skull_3, golden_apple_1), which is the same defect protocol 47 had with 1.13-flattened names: vanilla 1.12.2 names purple dye {item: minecraft:dye, data: 5} in its own assets/minecraft/recipes/purple_dye.json, and red wool {item: minecraft:wool, data: 14} in red_wool.json, so 'minecraft:dye_5' is a name the target server cannot round-trip through its own commands. The damage short is carried by ItemStackCodecs.ResolveLegacyItem as a damage component off the base composite and re-encodes byte-for-byte, so nothing is lost."
 },
 "identity": "legacy-composite",
 "identity_formula": "(item_id << 16) | damage",
